{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And you shall set the blessing.</b> This setting is with the mouth, in the manner of (Leviticus 16:21): ״ונתן אותם על ראש השעיר״." "<b>Upon Mount Gerizim.</b> Toward Mount Gerizim they would turn their faces and open with the blessing: 'Blessed is the man who does not make a carved or molten image,' and so with every 'cursed' in the parashah of Ki Tavo, they would first open with the language of 'blessed'; and afterward they would turn their faces toward Mount Eival and open with the curse." "<b>And the Ramban</b>, of blessed memory, wrote: it is possible that Mount Gerizim was to the south, which is the right side, and Mount Eival to the north, for (Jeremiah 1:14): ״מצפון תפתח הרעה״ — 'from the north the evil shall open.' End quote."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:46.313111471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}